Package: PhysioRehab
Title: ICF-Native Single-Case Clinical-Reasoning Tools for Rehabilitation
Version: 0.4.3
Authors@R:
    person("Yusuke", "Matsui", email = "mail.to.matsui@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Re-centres physiological measurement around the way rehabilitation
    reasons about the individual: International Classification of Functioning
    (ICF) semantics, individualised goal-referenced outcomes (Goal Attainment
    Scaling), single-case change detection that fuses quantitative signals with
    qualitative ICF qualifiers, a hypothesis-to-evidence reasoning scaffold that
    keeps the clinician in the loop, and an auto-drafted, ICF-structured progress
    note. Adapters ingest real signals from the ecosystem (markerless gait from
    'PhysioMoCap', muscle fatigue from 'PhysioEMG'); the ICF layer resolves
    against 'PhysioAnnotationHub'; single-case statistics come from 'PhysioAppKit'.
    The worked instance is stroke hemiplegic gait; the framework is
    condition-agnostic. A research tool with synthetic examples, not a medical
    device: outputs are clinician-in-the-loop measurement, documentation and
    reasoning support, never diagnosis.
